cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use JANUS in academic or commercial work, please cite the software using the metadata below."
type: software
title: "JANUS: A Decision Pipeline with Bounded LLM Authority for Algorithmic Trading"
abstract: >
  JANUS is a modular trading-bot pipeline that ranks candidate actions
  with the AGOP decision engine, gates candidate signals with KAIROS and
  Causalitybot, and passes the result to an open-source LLM whose only
  authority is to reduce or veto the position. Every emitted intent is
  checked against nine formal invariants (I1-I9) enforced by a
  design-by-contract verifier; a violation returns a flat intent at
  size zero. Optional subsystems include quantum econophysics modules
  (Baaquie tunneling, Ising herding) with exact classical fallbacks,
  opportunity modules that invert the interpretation of signal sources,
  and STIRPES, a unidirectional phylogenetic classifier that commits
  decision fingerprints to a settlement layer. The package ships a
  paper broker; live execution is out of scope.
